+# Higgs normalization audit
+
+This directory is an **additive research workspace**. It does not replace, rename, or modify any existing Cathedral file.
+
+## Exact finite-operator outputs
+
+The Cathedral finite Dirac audit fixes
+
+\[
+\Delta=\frac{3}{20}-\frac{(1-1/81)\pi}{13\phi},
+\qquad \phi=\frac{1+\sqrt5}{2},
+\]
+
+and
+
+\[
+a(\Delta)=\operatorname{Tr}(Y^\dagger Y)
+=\frac{16}{75}\left(100+183\Delta^2\right),
+\]
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+b(\Delta)&=\operatorname{Tr}\!\left[(Y^\dagger Y)^2\right]\\
+&=\frac{976}{27}+\frac{384}{5}\Delta
++\frac{99584}{225}\Delta^2
++\frac{1728}{5}\Delta^3
++\frac{420592}{1875}\Delta^4.
+\end{aligned}
+\]
+
+Numerically,
+
+\[
+a=21.33357522775238\ldots,
+\qquad
+b=36.34206561805763\ldots,
+\]
+
+so
+
+\[
+\boxed{
+\rho_H=\frac{b}{a^2}=0.07985136067642659\ldots
+}
+\]
+
+is the basis-independent Higgs shape invariant fixed by the finite operator.
+
+## Gauge trace
+
+For one Standard-Model generation of particle states,
+
+\[
+k_Y=\frac{10}{3},\qquad k_2=2,\qquad k_3=2,
+\]
+
+hence
+
+\[
+k_Y:k_2:k_3=\frac53:1:1.
+\]
+
+The canonical bare spectral boundary is therefore
+
+\[
+g_3^2=g_2^2=\frac53g_1^2,
+\qquad
+\sin^2\theta_W=\frac38.
+\]
+
+This means the older Cathedral value \(3/13\) is not the bare gauge coefficient of the canonical finite trace. It must arise through a separately derived normalization, running, or threshold mechanism.
+
+## Canonical normalization without assuming the prefactor
+
+Write one declared bosonic trace convention as
+
+\[
+\mathcal L_{\rm bos}
+=A_Wf_0k_2W^2+A_Hf_0a|DH|^2-A_Vf_0b|H|^4.
+\]
+
+Gauge normalization gives
+
+\[
+A_Wf_0k_2=\frac{1}{4g_2^2},
+\]
+
+and canonical scalar normalization gives
+
+\[
+H_c=\sqrt{A_Hf_0a}\,H.
+\]
+
+Therefore
+
+\[
+\boxed{
+\frac{\lambda_H}{g_2^2}
+=C_{\rm norm}\frac{b}{a^2},
+\qquad
+C_{\rm norm}=\frac{4k_2A_WA_V}{A_H^2}
+}
+\]
+
+The finite operator fixes \(b/a^2\). The physical quartic additionally requires all three action coefficients to be derived in one fixed convention.
+
+## Diagnostic against the old Cathedral slots
+
+Using
+
+\[
+\alpha_{\rm root}^{-1}=137.035999178195\ldots,
+\qquad
+\sin^2\theta_W=\frac3{13},
+\]
+
+gives
+
+\[
+g_2^2=0.397372026247011\ldots .
+\]
+
+The old quartic slot is
+
+\[
+\lambda_{\rm slot}=\frac18+\frac1{243}
+=0.12911522633744857\ldots .
+\]
+
+Exact equality would require
+
+\[
+\boxed{C_{\rm norm}=4.069095184887046\ldots}
+\]
+
+A convention with \(C_{\rm norm}=4\) yields
+
+\[
+\lambda_H=0.126922787962290\ldots,
+\]
+
+which is \(1.69805\%\) below the old slot. This is a near match, not an exact closure.
+
+## Status
+
+Closed:
+
+- the finite Dirac quadratic and quartic traces;
+- the invariant \(b/a^2\);
+- the bare gauge trace ratio \(5/3:1:1\);
+- the exact normalization identity in terms of \(A_W,A_H,A_V\).
+
+Open:
+
+- deriving \(A_W,A_H,A_V\) from one fully declared spectral-action convention;
+- fixing the physical trace domain, including conjugate and Majorana sectors;
+- specifying the boundary scale and RG evolution;
+- deriving the mechanism that connects the bare \(3/8\) boundary to the older \(3/13\) value.
