+# Chronology
+
+## 2026-07-13 — rails and structural sorting
+
+The central clarification was frozen:
+
+- `delta_star` is the lowest branch of the logistic-map cycle.
+- `delta_classic` is the neighbouring classical rail near `0.150`.
+- Their difference is the stability window, not an arbitrary correction.
+
+The original URTF description was separated from later Cathedral interpretation. The aim remained a direct, non-iterative, deterministic framework with no hand-picked slots.
+
+## 2026-07-14 — source recovery and adversarial audits
+
+The logistic verification report and the pi-phi-e flow report were recovered. Two audits were produced:
+
+1. A target-free estimator sweep showed that the archived raw estimator does not select `0.1475` or `0.150`; the later refinement explicitly attracts values toward `0.15`.
+2. The archived tanh operator was solved exactly. It has a superstable zero and unstable amplitude separatrices, but neither rail is a bifurcation in the parameter `delta`.
+
+These negative results are retained because they prevent circular derivations from re-entering the framework.
+
+## 2026-07-15 to 2026-07-19 — consolidation state
+
+The rail semantics, gap-as-bandwidth interpretation, scalar root coupling, entropy-scale map, hidden `A5` sector, and physical-action requirements were consolidated. No additional target-free derivation of the rail-selection parameter was established in the accessible record.
+
+## 2026-07-20 — finite Dirac/Higgs trace audit
+
+The charge-word matrices were traced exactly. The matrix invariant
+
+`G2 / Y2^2 = 0.128356357761657...`
+
+was verified. It lies close to, but is not exactly equal to, the earlier Cathedral quartic slot
+
+`1/8 + 1/243 = 0.129115226337449...`.
+
+The difference is about `0.587745%`.
+
+The physical Higgs coupling did not close because the gauge kinetic coefficient, scalar kinetic coefficient, quartic coefficient, trace domain, and boundary scale must all be obtained from the same action. A convention-dependent prefactor may not be inserted after the trace calculation.
