+# Frozen definitions
+
+## Geometric constants
+
+\[
+D=3,\quad V=12,\quad E=30,\quad F=20,\quad q=5,\quad N=13,\quad G=60,
+\]
+
+\[
+\phi=\frac{1+\sqrt5}{2},\qquad \gamma=\frac1{81}.
+\]
+
+## Rail semantics
+
+The semantic definition is:
+
+\[
+\boxed{\delta_\star=\text{lowest branch of the selected attracting logistic-map cycle}.}
+\]
+
+The classical rail is
+
+\[
+\boxed{\delta_{\rm cl}=\frac3{20}=0.15.}
+\]
+
+The stability bandwidth is
+
+\[
+\boxed{\Delta=\delta_{\rm cl}-\delta_\star.}
+\]
+
+## Two numerical realizations currently in the record
+
+### Algebraic/geometric realization
+
+\[
+\delta_\star^{\rm geom}
+=\left(1-\frac1{81}\right)\frac{\pi}{13\phi}
+=0.14751081015957962\ldots
+\]
+
+which gives
+
+\[
+\Delta_{\rm geom}
+=0.002489189840420375\ldots
+\]
+
+### Logistic-cycle realization at the archived target parameter
+
+At
+
+\[
+r_{\rm target}=3.8417002878419497,
+\]
+
+the two lowest branches recorded in the verification report are
+
+\[
+\delta_\star^{\rm cycle}=0.1474219361622878,
+\]
+
+\[
+\delta_{\rm cl}^{\rm cycle}=0.1500067276982269,
+\]
+
+with split
+
+\[
+\Delta_{\rm cycle}=0.0025847915359391016.
+\]
+
+## Unresolved identity condition
+
+The archived geometric and logistic values differ by
+
+\[
+\delta_\star^{\rm geom}-\delta_\star^{\rm cycle}
+=8.887399729182177\times10^{-5}.
+\]
+
+Therefore the statement that the geometric closed form is *exactly* the archived logistic branch is not presently true for the numbers retained here. The framework must either:
+
+- derive a different logistic parameter at which the lower branch equals the geometric value;
+- revise the algebraic expression;
+- or treat the agreement as approximate rather than exact.
+
+This discrepancy is frozen as an open issue and must not be hidden by rounding both values to `0.1475`.
