+# Entropy scale and scalar root coupling
+
+This file records the frozen carry-in equations used during the week.
+
+## Minimal scalar residue
+
+With
+
+\[
+W_{\rm scalar}=\frac95,
+\qquad
+S_{\rm ent}=\frac{1+\gamma}{D}=\frac{82}{243},
+\qquad
+S_{\rm exh}=\frac{N-D-1}{qN}=\frac9{65},
+\]
+
+the scalar inverse-coupling polynomial is
+
+\[
+\boxed{
+\alpha_{\rm root}^{-1}
+=137+\frac{17572}{1215}\Delta-\frac9{65}\Delta^2.
+}
+\]
+
+Using the geometric bandwidth,
+
+\[
+\boxed{
+\alpha_{\rm root}^{-1}=137.035999178195\ldots
+}
+\]
+
+This arithmetic identity is verified. Its identification with the physical electromagnetic coupling remains a physical theorem to be justified by the action and representation, not by numerical agreement alone.
+
+## Metric entropy projection
+
+The proposed projection from total entropy depth `eta` to metric entropy `sigma` is
+
+\[
+\boxed{d\sigma=\frac{N-D}{N}d\eta=\frac{10}{13}d\eta.}
+\]
+
+Hence
+
+\[
+\sigma=\frac{10}{13}\eta,
+\qquad
+\frac{\mu}{\mu_C}=e^{-\sigma},
+\qquad
+\beta_{\rm scale}=\frac{13}{10}.
+\]
+
+The corresponding entropy-form running equation is
+
+\[
+\frac{d\alpha_i^{-1}}{d\eta}
+=\frac{10}{13}\frac{b_i}{2\pi}.
+\]
+
+## Recorded entropy landmarks
+
+Using the geometric gap:
+
+\[
+\eta_W=\delta_\star,
+\qquad
+\eta_\Delta=-\ln\Delta,
+\qquad
+\eta_{\rm conf}=\frac{13}{10}\frac{169\pi}{70},
+\qquad
+\eta_{\rm IR}=-\phi^2\ln\Delta.
+\]
+
+The proposed hierarchy is
+
+\[
+\eta_W<\eta_\Delta<\eta_{\rm conf}<\eta_{\rm IR}.
+\]
+
+## Status
+
+- scalar polynomial arithmetic: **VERIFIED**;
+- `10/13` entropy projection as an internally stated rule: **FROZEN / CONDITIONAL**;
+- identification with physical RG scale: **OPEN**;
+- electromagnetic identification of the scalar singlet: **OPEN PHYSICAL STEP**.
