+# Gap field, A5 cone, and hidden sector
+
+## Gap as bandwidth
+
+The week retained the interpretation
+
+\[
+\Delta=\delta_{\rm cl}-\delta_\star
+\]
+
+as more than a numerical residual. It is the width of the lower dynamical rail pair and therefore a candidate bandwidth in which an effective field can live.
+
+The roles currently assigned to the gap include:
+
+- stability bandwidth between lower rails;
+- small universal correction scale;
+- source for light-sector mass splittings;
+- possible field-support interval;
+- bridge between dynamical and geometric descriptions.
+
+These roles must ultimately be derived from a single operator. Reusing the same small number in several formulas is not itself proof that the roles are identical.
+
+## Visible and hidden representation sectors
+
+The retained A5 decomposition includes a hidden eight-dimensional sector
+
+\[
+\ker(B^T)\cong \mathbf4\oplus\mathbf4.
+\]
+
+The visible centred-icosahedral sectors contain scalar, triplet, conjugate triplet, and five-dimensional components. The working proposal is that the hidden `4+4` sector supports a shadow cone complementary to the visible cone.
+
+## Shadow-cone proposal
+
+The shadow cone and its connection to the dark sector are currently a hypothesis with the following required structure:
+
+1. a projector onto the hidden `4+4` subspace;
+2. a quadratic form defining its cone;
+3. a coupling operator between visible and hidden sectors;
+4. positivity/unitarity conditions;
+5. a derivation of any dark-sector observables from the hidden propagator.
+
+No unique shadow-cone metric or Lagrangian was derived in the accessible weekly record. The idea is preserved as **OPEN**, not deleted.
