+# Finite Dirac and Higgs trace audit
+
+## A/B charge-word construction
+
+Let
+
+\[
+a=\frac{\phi}{\sqrt3},\qquad b=\frac1{\sqrt3\phi},
+\]
+
+\[
+A=\begin{pmatrix}a&0&0\\0&b&0\\0&0&0\end{pmatrix},
+\qquad
+B=\begin{pmatrix}0&0&-b\\0&0&0\\0&-a&0\end{pmatrix}.
+\]
+
+The exact golden-ratio identities give
+
+\[
+a^2+b^2=1,
+\qquad
+ab=\frac13,
+\qquad
+A\perp B
+\]
+
+in the Frobenius inner product.
+
+For
+
+\[
+T=pA+qB,
+\qquad S=p^2+q^2,
+\]
+
+one obtains
+
+\[
+\boxed{\operatorname{tr}(TT^\dagger)=S}
+\]
+
+and
+
+\[
+\boxed{
+\operatorname{tr}[(TT^\dagger)^2]
+=\frac{7S^2-10p^2q^2}{9}.
+}
+\]
+
+These identities are exact.
+
+## Aggregated particle-sector trace
+
+Using the four archived charge words and colour multiplicities gives
+
+\[
+Y_2=33.8869774978071\ldots,
+\]
+
+\[
+G_2=147.395102550220\ldots,
+\]
+
+and the normalized shape invariant
+
+\[
+\boxed{
+\mathcal R_H=\frac{G_2}{Y_2^2}
+=0.128356357761657\ldots
+}
+\]
+
+For the particle-only off-diagonal finite matrix,
+
+\[
+D_F=\begin{pmatrix}0&M\\M^\dagger&0\end{pmatrix},
+\]
+
+this is equivalent to
+
+\[
+2\frac{\operatorname{Tr}D_F^4}{(\operatorname{Tr}D_F^2)^2}
+=\mathcal R_H.
+\]
+
+## Comparison with the earlier slot
+
+The earlier slot was
+
+\[
+\lambda_{\rm slot}=\frac18+\frac1{243}
+=0.129115226337449\ldots
+\]
+
+The relative discrepancy is
+
+\[
+\boxed{0.587745\%}.
+\]
+
+This is a near match, not exact equality.
+
+## Structural defect of the simplified matrices
+
+Each matrix `T=pA+qB` has
+
+\[
+\det T=0,
+\]
+
+so it is generically rank two. If interpreted literally as a three-generation Yukawa matrix, it leaves one zero singular value in each fermion sector. It is therefore a skeleton or reduced charge operator, not yet a complete physical Yukawa matrix.
+
+## Physical normalization requirement
+
+The physical quartic must be derived from one declared bosonic action,
+
+\[
+\mathcal L
+=K_W W_{\mu\nu}W^{\mu\nu}
++K_H(D_\mu H)^\dagger(D^\mu H)
+-V_H(H^\dagger H)^2.
+\]
+
+After canonical normalization,
+
+\[
+g_2^{-2}=4K_W,
+\qquad
+H_c=\sqrt{K_H}H,
+\qquad
+\boxed{\lambda_H=\frac{V_H}{K_H^2}}.
+\]
+
+The same trace domain, generator convention, scalar normalization, and boundary scale must determine all three coefficients. Therefore `g2=1` or a prefactor such as `2` or `4` cannot be inserted without deriving it from that action.
+
+## Provisional full-operator formula retained separately
+
+A later provisional record introduced
+
+\[
+a_{\rm full}(\Delta)=\frac{16}{75}(100+183\Delta^2)
+\]
+
+and a quartic polynomial `b_full(Delta)` giving
+
+\[
+\frac{b_{\rm full}}{a_{\rm full}^2}
+=0.07985136067642659\ldots
+\]
+
+These formulae are preserved in `newtons_cathedral/higgs_normalization.py`, but their full derivation was not present in the accessible source record. Their status is **PROVISIONAL UNTIL SOURCE DERIVATION IS RECOVERED**.
