+# Next derivation
+
+The shortest non-circular route is:
+
+## Step 1 — derive the rail-selection equation
+
+Construct a scalar equation
+
+\[
+F(r;G_{13},\gamma,\phi)=0
+\]
+
+from the fixed geometry and dynamics, without inserting either rail value. It must have a unique admissible root inside the stable period-six interval. The logistic cycle is then computed from that root, and `delta_star` is defined as its lowest branch.
+
+This would remove the present circularity in which `r_target` is chosen to match a prior `delta_star`.
+
+## Step 2 — reconcile the two lower-rail values
+
+The theory must explain or remove
+
+\[
+8.887399729182177\times10^{-5}
+\]
+
+between the geometric formula and archived logistic branch. A successful closure must state whether the difference is:
+
+- a finite-discretization correction;
+- a flow-to-map renormalization;
+- an incorrect archived target parameter;
+- or evidence that the geometric formula is only approximate.
+
+## Step 3 — build the complete finite operator
+
+The operator must lift the rank-two null modes without fitted coefficients. Candidate lifts may depend only on already forced objects such as the gap, hidden-sector projector, chirality operator, or graph Laplacian.
+
+## Step 4 — derive the bosonic action in one convention
+
+Compute from the same finite Hilbert space:
+
+\[
+K_W,\qquad K_H,\qquad V_H.
+\]
+
+Then set
+
+\[
+g_2^{-2}=4K_W,
+\qquad
+\lambda_H=V_H/K_H^2.
+\]
+
+No external prefactor is allowed.
+
+## Step 5 — identify the boundary scale
+
+Use the entropy-scale map only after proving which entropy depth corresponds to the spectral boundary. Then run all couplings to a common physical scale before comparing with measured values.
+
+## Completion criterion
+
+The Higgs/rail sector is closed only when a single executable program starts from the fixed geometry and returns:
+
+1. `r_target`;
+2. the six-cycle and lower-rail split;
+3. the complete finite Dirac spectrum;
+4. gauge, scalar kinetic, and scalar quartic coefficients;
+5. the boundary scale and RG-evolved low-energy outputs;
+
+without target values, branch choices, fitted coefficients, or post-hoc normalization.
