+# Newton's Cathedral weekly research archive
+
+**Window:** 2026-07-13 through 2026-07-20  
+**Author:** Cornelius Lytollis  
+**Repository target:** `con123-gif/URT-Enhanced-v2.0`, default branch `newtons-cathedral`
+
+This directory preserves the work developed during the stated week without replacing or deleting any earlier Cathedral or URT material. It is intentionally additive.
+
+## Archive rules
+
+1. `delta_star` means the **lowest branch/value of the logistic-map attracting cycle**. This semantic definition takes precedence over older descriptions of it as merely a geometric candidate.
+2. `delta_classic = 3/20` is the classical rail.
+3. `Delta = delta_classic - delta_star` is the stability bandwidth/gap.
+4. Where the logistic branch and algebraic closed form differ numerically, both are retained and the difference is recorded rather than silently erased.
+5. Every result is labelled as `VERIFIED`, `CONDITIONAL`, `PROVISIONAL`, `OPEN`, or `SUPERSEDED`.
+6. No target-led fitting, selected branches, post-hoc coefficients, or hidden normalization choices may be promoted to a first-principles result.
+
+## Contents
+
+- `00_chronology.md` — work sequence and decisions.
+- `01_frozen_definitions.md` — constants and semantic definitions.
+- `02_logistic_rails.md` — stable six-cycle result and rail discrepancy.
+- `03_urt_operator_audits.md` — target-free and separatrix audits.
