+# Reconstructed source note: URT Logistic Map Verification
+
+Original uploaded title: `URT_Logistic_Map_Verification.pdf`  
+Original report date: 2026-04-22  
+Recovered into the weekly archive: 2026-07-14
+
+The report identifies an attracting six-cycle of the logistic map at
+
+`r = 3.8417002878419497`
+
+with ordered branches:
+
+1. `0.1474219361622878`
+2. `0.1500067276982269`
+3. `0.4828583491613422`
+4. `0.4898348785861162`
+5. `0.9592962413714381`
+6. `0.9600281102477677`
+
+It reports Lyapunov exponent `-0.011275`; the weekly direct cycle-multiplier audit gives `-0.011252611976695...`. Both are negative. The report interprets the lower pair as the split of the lowest period-three branch after period doubling.
+
+The report also records that `r_target` was not found to be a simple low-degree algebraic number and was selected by matching the lower branch to a prior URT value. This selection dependence is preserved as an open issue.
