+# Reconstructed source note: pi-phi-e flow
+
+Original uploaded title: `pi_phi_e_flow.pdf`  
+Original report date: April 2026  
+Recovered into the weekly archive: 2026-07-14
+
+The report proposes a continuous field equation on a 13-site centred icosahedral graph:
+
+\[
+\partial_t\delta
+=-\frac1{4\pi}L\delta
+-(\phi-1)e^{-t/10}(\delta-\delta_\star)(1+\delta^2).
+\]
+
+It uses
+
+\[
+\delta_\star=(1-1/81)\frac{\pi}{13\phi}
+\]
+
+and describes the working URT update as an Euler discretization with approximate coefficients.
+
+Weekly audit note: the report's uniqueness statements and coefficient-forcing claims require proof beyond the supplied text. In addition, its graph spectrum differs from other centred-icosahedral spectra recorded elsewhere in the project and must be reconciled before it can serve as the definitive operator source.
